ProtocolFeeCollector::distribute
├── given PAUSE_TYPE is paused
│   ├── it should revert with IsPaused
│   └── it should not harvest configured sources
└── given PAUSE_TYPE is not paused
    ├── it should be callable by any address
    ├── before calculating collected and the split
    │   ├── it should harvest registered borrow markets in registry order
    │   ├── it should harvest registered mint markets in registry order
    │   ├── it should harvest registered USMs in registry order
    │   ├── it should harvest the configured flash minter last
    │   ├── it should include all successfully harvested DUSD in collected
    │   ├── it should emit Harvested for valid sources including zero-fee sources
    │   ├── when a configured source is invalid or a market is paused
    │   │   ├── it should emit HarvestingFailed without emitting Harvested for that source
    │   │   └── it should continue harvesting later configured sources
    │   ├── when a valid source execution reverts
    │   │   ├── it should propagate the revert
    │   │   └── it should roll back earlier harvests and distribution
    │   └── when a registry getter reverts
    │       └── it should propagate the revert
    ├── when the calculated rewardAmount is zero
    │   ├── it should not require the sDUSD vault to be set
    │   ├── it should not check rewardPeriodFinish
    │   ├── when nonzero rewardsBps rounds rewardAmount down to zero, it should still skip the vault checks
    │   ├── it should not apply minimumRewardAmount or call notifyRewardAmount
    │   ├── it should transfer all nonzero collected DUSD, including harvested DUSD, to the treasury
    │   ├── it should emit Distributed with a zero reward amount
    │   └── when the post-harvest collector DUSD balance is zero
    │       ├── it should not transfer DUSD to the treasury
    │       └── it should emit Distributed with zero amounts
    └── when the calculated rewardAmount is nonzero
        ├── when rewardAmount is below minimumRewardAmount
        │   ├── it should retain the complete post-harvest balance in the collector
        │   ├── it should not transfer the treasury allocation or notify the vault
        │   ├── it should not require the vault to be configured or its reward period to be finished
        │   ├── it should emit DistributionDeferred without emitting Distributed
        │   └── it should allow retained funds and later harvests to accumulate until the minimum is met
        └── when rewardAmount is at least minimumRewardAmount
            ├── when rewardAmount equals minimumRewardAmount
            │   └── it should allow distribution
            ├── when the sDUSD vault is not set
            │   ├── it should revert with ProtocolFeeCollectorSdusdNotSet
            │   └── it should leave the treasury allocation in the collector
            ├── when the sDUSD reward period has not finished
            │   ├── it should revert with ProtocolFeeCollectorRewardPeriodNotFinished
            │   └── it should leave the treasury allocation in the collector
            └── when the sDUSD reward period has finished
                ├── when block timestamp equals rewardPeriodFinish
                │   └── it should allow distribution
                ├── when the sDUSD vault is paused
                │   ├── it should revert with IsPaused
                │   └── it should leave the treasury allocation in the collector
                ├── when the configured sDUSD vault has not received its required seed deposit
                │   ├── it should revert with SDUSDNotSeeded
                │   └── it should leave the treasury allocation in the collector
                ├── when only the locked seed shares remain in the sDUSD vault
                │   ├── it should revert with SDUSDNoActiveStakers
                │   └── it should leave the treasury allocation in the collector
                ├── when the collector is not the sDUSD vault's configured rewarder
                │   ├── it should revert with SDUSDNotRewarder
                │   └── it should leave the treasury allocation in the collector
                ├── when rewardsBps equals PERCENTAGE_PRECISION
                │   ├── it should not transfer DUSD to the treasury
                │   ├── it should notify the configured sDUSD vault of all collected DUSD
                │   ├── it should reset the sDUSD allowance to zero
                │   └── it should emit Distributed with a zero treasury amount
                └── when rewardsBps is between zero and PERCENTAGE_PRECISION
                    ├── it should calculate rewardAmount by rounding down
                    ├── it should calculate treasuryAmount as collected minus rewardAmount
                    ├── it should transfer treasuryAmount to the configured treasury
                    ├── it should approve only rewardAmount to the configured sDUSD vault
                    ├── it should call notifyRewardAmount with rewardAmount
                    ├── it should reset the sDUSD allowance to zero
                    ├── it should leave the collector with zero distributed DUSD
                    └── it should emit Distributed with the collected, treasury, and reward amounts
